  pattern: EVERY items 20, COUNT items 13; items whose DRIFT entry is O: ['Mahler1968', 'Akin2004', 'InHouseBCD']
  every COUNT item is DEFECT-blind.  Among the EVERY items about integers or single orbits, the Diophantine /
  transversality ones (Senge-Straus, Stewart, Dimitrov-Howe, Yu, Ren-Roettger, Knight, Theorem S) exclude only
  zero-entropy classes (few nonzero digits, bounded p-adic closeness, short top runs, Christoffel or Sturmian
  words).  The two that constrain positive-entropy classes of parity words (Monks-Yazinski 2.7(b): subcritical
  density; InHouseBCD: bounded critical discrepancy) use growth and capacity, not 2-versus-3 transversality, and
  work only where the orbit would shrink or grow at most linearly.  Supercritical positive-entropy words: nothing.

S3.0 FINITE-EXACT engines
  Erdos scan 0<=K<=200000: K without ternary digit 2: [0, 2, 8]; deepest lowest-2 position 29 at K=159140; full conversions 3
  base-5 analogue 0<=K<=200000: K with all base-5 digits of 2^K in {0,1}: [0]
  ternary profile 50<=K<=20000: min nonzero proportion 0.5429 (K=54), min digit-2 proportion 0.2083 (K=76), min #nonzero 19 (K=54), longest 0-run 15 (K=12398), longest run 18 (K=5677)
  low-digit classes N_j = #{K mod 2*3^(j-1): lowest j ternary digits of 2^K in {0,1}}: {1: 1, 2: 2, 3: 4, 4: 8, 5: 16, 6: 32, 7: 64, 8: 128, 9: 256, 10: 512, 11: 1024, 12: 2048, 13: 4096, 14: 8192, 15: 16384, 16: 32768}  (= 2^(j-1), PROVED; brute force agrees for small j)
  kappa identity v_3(2^K b - a) = [K=e mod 2](1 + v_3(K - kappa(a/b))) verified for K <= 3000:
     r=1/1: e=0, kappa = ...0 (base 3, low digits last), max v_3 = inf
     r=1/2: e=1, kappa = ...222222222222 (base 3, low digits last), max v_3 = 7
