                         3n-1: n/a | 5n+1: (5/2)^n: range >= 1/5: PROVED (same theorem, 1/p) | DEFECT: sees (EVERY) | INTEGRAL: n/a | UNIFORM: n/a
  H3                   | xi(3/2)^n    | dist  | all    | OPEN    | for every xi > 0, limsup - liminf of frac(xi (3/2)^n) > 1/2
                         evidence: would imply T4
                         3n-1: ratio -3/2: OPEN (Lu-Zheng 2026 prove spread >= 11/27) | 5n+1: ratio 5/2: spread > 1/2 for every xi: FALSE: Z_{5/2}-numbers exist (p = 5 > q^2 = 4; Tijdeman 1972, Flatto 1992 [R via Andrieu-Eliahou-Vivion]) | DEFECT: sees (EVERY) | INTEGRAL: n/a | UNIFORM: n/a
  H4                   | xi(3/2)^n    | digit | all    | OPEN    | for every xi > 0 there is n with frac(xi (3/2)^n) >= 1/2
                         evidence: Mahler 1968 (= no Z-number)
                         3n-1: n/a | 5n+1: ratio 5/2: FALSE: Z_{5/2}-numbers exist (p = 5 > q^2 = 4; Tijdeman 1972, Flatto 1992 [R via Andrieu-Eliahou-Vivion]) | DEFECT: sees (EVERY) | INTEGRAL: n/a | UNIFORM: n/a
  H5                   | xi(3/2)^n    | dist  | almost | PROVED  | for almost every xi > 0, (xi (3/2)^n) is uniformly distributed mod 1
                         evidence: Koksma 1935 (classical metric theorem) [R]
                         3n-1: n/a | 5n+1: n/a | DEFECT: blind (COUNT) | INTEGRAL: n/a | UNIFORM: n/a
  H6                   | xi(3/2)^n    | dist  | all    | PROVED  | ||(3/2)^n|| > (3/4)^n for all n >= n0 (ineffective)
                         evidence: Mahler 1957, Mathematika 4, 122-124 (with Corvaja-Zannier 2004, Zudilin 2007) [R]
                         3n-1: n/a | 5n+1: n/a | DEFECT: sees (EVERY) | INTEGRAL: n/a | UNIFORM: n/a
  H7                   | xi(3/2)^n    | digit | all    | PROVED  | each interval [m, m+1) contains at most one Z-number (so they are countable)
                         evidence: Mahler 1968, J. Austral. Math. Soc. 8, 313-321 [P]
                         3n-1: n/a | 5n+1: n/a | DEFECT: sees (EVERY) | INTEGRAL: n/a | UNIFORM: n/a
  H8                   | xi(3/2)^n    | digit | all    | PROVED  | no Z-number lies below the Dubickas-Mossinghoff bound
                         evidence: Dubickas-Mossinghoff 2009, Math. Comp. 78, 1837-1851 [R]
                         3n-1: n/a | 5n+1: n/a | DEFECT: sees (EVERY) | INTEGRAL: n/a | UNIFORM: n/a

S3.2 Statement x target matrix  (<=> equivalent, => implies, =>c conditional, part = PROVED/OPEN partial (excludes a thin class of counterexamples), . none).  Status column: PRV/FIN/OPN/FLS.
  id                     status     T1    T2    T3    T4    PC   blocked-by (where the relation is part/none)
  A1                     OPN         .     .   <=>     .     .
  A2                     PRV         .     .     .     .     .   T3: DEFECT: a counting statement allows a sparse exceptional set
  A3                     PRV         .     .     .     .     .   T3: DEFECT
  A4                     PRV         .     .  part     .     .   T3: bounded complexity only: excludes counterexamples with <= 25 ternary ones
  B1[D=1]                FLS         .     .     .     .     .   T3: INTEGRAL: periodic in K mod 2*3^(D-1); the 3-adic window cannot see the size of 2^K; T2: INTEGRAL: same periodicity
  B2[D=1]                FLS         .     .     .     .     .   T3: INTEGRAL; T2: INTEGRAL
  B1[D=13]               FLS         .     .     .     .     .   T3: INTEGRAL: periodic in K mod 2*3^(D-1); the 3-adic window cannot see the size of 2^K; T2: INTEGRAL: same periodicity
  B2[D=13]               FLS         .     .     .     .     .   T3: INTEGRAL; T2: INTEGRAL
  C1                     PRV         .     .     .     .     .   T3: DIM: excludes only a zero-dimensional exceptional set; T3's set has dimension log_3 2
  C2                     OPN         .     .     .     .     .   T3: does not force the digit 2
  C3                     PRV         .     .     .     .     .   T3: DEFECT
  R1                     PRV         .     .  part     .     .   T3: a short top run does not force a digit 2
  R2                     PRV         .  part     .     .     .   T3: 3-adic window (INTEGRAL); T2: the landing needs all hostile balls, not only 1 and -1
  R3                     OPN         .     .     .     .     .   T3: does not force a digit 2
  D1                     FLS         .     .     .     .     .   T2: INTEGRAL: 1 is a 3-adic limit point of 2^K
  D2                     PRV         .  part     .     .     .   T2: controls one terminal landing (fixed w_final); not the adversarial chain
  D3                     OPN         .  part     .     .     .   T2: as D2
  D4                     PRV         .     .     .     .     .   T2: DEFECT
  E1                     FLS         .     .     .     .     .   T2: equidistribution forces hostile landings; T2 needs chain steering
  E2                     PRV         .     .     .     .     .   T2: DEFECT: the adversary picks the chain
  E3                     OPN         .   <=>     .     .     .
  F1                     PRV         .     .     .     .     .   T1: DIM
  F2                     PRV         .     .     .     .     .   T1: DIM
  F3                     FLS         .     .     .     .     .
  F4                     OPN         .     .     .     .     .
