S3.3 Minimal unblocked statements per target: statements that imply the target, are not FALSE, and are not blocked; among them the weakest (<=> before =>, conditional last).  PROVED partial results listed separately.
  T1: no divergent positive 3x+1 orbit (Periodicity for Z^+, k=1): Phi(w) not in Z^+ for every non-EP word w
     <=>  G[HARD].notZ+.all: for every w in HARD (non-EP words outside SUB, BCD, STURM and REP), Phi(w) is not a positive integer  [OPEN] | 3n-1 analogue: OPEN | 5n+1 analogue: OPEN (expected FALSE: K-L)
     <=>  G[ALL].notZ+.all: for every w in ALL (all non-EP words), Phi(w) is not a positive integer  [OPEN] | 3n-1 analogue: OPEN | 5n+1 analogue: OPEN (expected FALSE: Kontorovich-Lagarias)
     =>   G[ALL].irr.all: for every w in ALL (all non-EP words), Phi(w) is irrational  [OPEN] | 3n-1 analogue: OPEN | 5n+1 analogue: OPEN (expected FALSE)
     PROVED partial: G[STURM].irr.all; G[SUB].irr.all; G[BCD].notZ+.all; G[REP].irr.all
  T2: E-SCC Q2 endgame (loops_and_escapes sec. 8): every hostile see-saw chain ends at 2^K w_final in a descending class
     <=>  E3: every hostile see-saw chain ends at a landing 2^K w_final in a descending class (steering statement)  [OPEN] | 3n-1 analogue: OPEN | 5n+1 analogue: OPEN (untested)
     PROVED partial: R2; D2
  T3: Erdos: 2^n has a ternary digit 2 for every n >= 9
     <=>  A1: for all K >= 9, 2^K has a ternary digit 2  [OPEN] | 5n+1 analogue: OPEN; FINITE-EXACT for 1<=K<=200000 (K with only digits 0,1: [0])
     PROVED partial: A4; R1
  T4: Mahler: there is no Z-number (Phi_M(S) contains no positive integer, THM-2228)
     <=>  H4: for every xi > 0 there is n with frac(xi (3/2)^n) >= 1/2  [OPEN] | 5n+1 analogue: FALSE: Z_{5/2}-numbers exist (p = 5 > q^2 = 4; Tijdeman 1972, Flatto 1992 [R via Andrieu-Eliahou-Vivion])
     <=>  M1: for every carry word c in S (safe: all tails Y_n(c) < 1), Phi_M(c) is not a positive integer  [OPEN] | 5n+1 analogue: FALSE: Z_{5/2}-numbers exist (p = 5 > q^2 = 4; Tijdeman 1972, Flatto 1992 [R via Andrieu-Eliahou-Vivion])
     =>   H3: for every xi > 0, limsup - liminf of frac(xi (3/2)^n) > 1/2  [OPEN] | 3n-1 analogue: OPEN (Lu-Zheng 2026 prove spread >= 11/27) | 5n+1 analogue: FALSE: Z_{5/2}-numbers exist (p = 5 > q^2 = 4; Tijdeman 1972, Flatto 1992 [R via Andrieu-Eliahou-Vivion])
     PROVED partial: M2; H2; H7; H8
  PC: Lagarias's Periodicity Conjecture: Phi(w) irrational for every non-EP word w (all 3x+k, k = +-1 mod 6)
     <=>  G[ALL].irr.all: for every w in ALL (all non-EP words), Phi(w) is irrational  [OPEN] | 3n-1 analogue: OPEN | 5n+1 analogue: OPEN (expected FALSE)
     PROVED partial: G[STURM].irr.all; G[SUB].irr.all; G[BCD].irr.all; G[REP].irr.all

